course: dictionary
lesson: 15001
title: Rerun: when something happens again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rerun is when something is shown, run or done again. The word is made of «re-», which means again, and «run». In everyday life, the most common rerun is a TV programme or film shown a second time. «The channel showed a rerun of the old cartoon after tea.» The clues are «after tea» and «old»: the cartoon was shown before, so rerun means shown again.
explain: Rerun can also be a verb, a doing word. «The teacher asked us to rerun the test because the computer crashed.» Rerun here means to do the test again. To check your meaning, swap «do again» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: In science and computing, you rerun an experiment or a program to check the results are right. In sport, a race can be rerun after a false start, when someone starts too early and the race has to begin again. Look at the words around rerun to see which meaning fits.
fact: A rerun is a noun (a rerun, reruns) when it names something shown again.
fact: Rerun is a verb (rerun, reruns, reran, rerunning) when it means to do something again.
fact: «A rerun» means a TV programme or film shown again.
fact: «Rerun the race» means run the race again, for example after a false start.
fact: Something that happens again in the same way can also be called a rerun.
exercise: «The old comedy show was a rerun from last year.» What is a rerun here? | A brand new show never seen before | A large wooden box | A kind of sports shoe | *A show shown again
exercise: The scientist decided to rerun the experiment to check the result. What does rerun mean here? | To stop it for ever | To hide it | *To do it again | To paint it red
exercise: Find the word in «The race was rerun after a false start» that means run again. | start | *rerun | false | race
test: «The programme is a rerun of last winter's show.» What does rerun mean? | Made for the first time | Lost forever | *Shown again | Cancelled before it started
test: Mr Patel had to ___ the test after the computer crashed. Which word fills the gap? | hide | *rerun | forget | cancel
exam: Which sentence uses rerun as a noun, meaning something shown again? | «She reran the test twice.» | «We will rerun the race at noon.» | *«The rerun of the film made us laugh again.» | «They are rerunning the program now.»
